usage: janus dead-letters [-h] [--environment ENVIRONMENT]
                          [--project-root PROJECT_ROOT]
                          {list,release,replay} ...

Inspect, release or replay the items a source's runs gave up on. Nothing runs
unless replay is given --execute.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --environment ENVIRONMENT
                        Environment profile name under conf/environments
                        without the .yaml suffix.
  --project-root PROJECT_ROOT
                        Project root used to resolve conf/ and data/ paths.

actions:
  {list,release,replay}
    list                Print a source's dead letters, each with its error and
                        metadata.
    release             Release dead letters with a recorded reason, so the
                        next resuming run retries them.
    replay              Show what a resume would retry after a release (a dry
                        run, the default), or release and run it with
                        --execute.

A dead letter is an item a run skipped after exhausting its retries. Every
action plans the source to find its metadata zone, disabled sources included.
Only replay with --execute reads an environment profile or runs anything.
`janus dead-letters ACTION --help` describes each action.
